==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gmh|de}} {{m|gmh|stube}}, from {{etym|goh|de}} {{term|stuba|lang=goh}}. Cognate with {{etyl|nl|-}} {{m|nl|stoof}}. Further origin uncertain. See {{term|stove|lang=en}} for more.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈʃtuːbə/|lang=de}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|f||Stuben|Stübchen|dim2=Stüblein}}

# {{context|regional|lang=de}} [[living room]]
# [[parlour]] {{gloss|a room used chiefly for representation purposes; often called {{term|gute Stube|lang=de}} or the like}}
# the [[heated]] part of a traditional [[farmhouse]] (as opposed to stables, kitchen, etc.)
# {{context|military|lang=de}} [[bedroom]] in a [[barracks]]

